1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,080
He sank a British battleship in the heart of the Royal Navy's most important base, and a year and a half later he vanished without a trace in the Atlantic.

2
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:10,140
His name was Günther Prien.

3
00:00:10,170 --> 00:00:16,540
He was born in Osterfeld in 1908 and went to sea as a teenager, first on a sailing ship.

4
00:00:16,630 --> 00:00:20,360
In the Great Depression he lost his job in the merchant navy.

5
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:23,830
He joined the Nazi party and entered the Reichsmarine.

6
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:27,460
When the war began he commanded the submarine U-47.

7
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:35,920
On the night of 14 October 1939 he slipped into Scapa Flow, the base of the British Home Fleet in the Orkney Islands.

8
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:39,420
He crept through a narrow channel between sunken blockships.

9
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:44,260
Most ships had left, but the battleship Royal Oak lay at anchor.

10
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:46,440
The first attack only hit the bow.

11
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:49,260
Prien had the tubes reloaded and attacked a second time.

12
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:51,290
This time three torpedoes hit.

13
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:54,450
The Royal Oak capsized within 13 minutes.

14
00:00:54,470 --> 00:01:00,110
835 men died, more than a hundred of them boys under 18.

15
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:02,960
U-47 escaped the same way it came.

16
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:08,490
In Berlin Hitler received the crew, and propaganda made Prien the Bull of Scapa Flow.

17
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:11,880
He went on to sink around 30 merchant ships in the Atlantic.

18
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,380
One of them was the Arandora Star.

19
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:20,330
She was carrying German and Italian internees to Canada; more than 800 people died.

20
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:26,100
In March 1941 U-47 attacked a convoy in the North Atlantic.

21
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:28,110
After that, no further radio message came.

22
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:31,460
The naval command kept the loss secret for more than ten weeks.

23
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:34,770
Soon rumours spread that Prien had disappeared into a penal camp.

24
00:01:34,910 --> 00:01:40,260
What happened to U-47 and its 45 men remains unresolved to this day.

25
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:43,020
Günther Prien was 33 years old.
